while it won't make you into Ironman  this exosuit can help you walk like one  researchers at the visa Institute in  Massachusetts have constructed a robotic  exoskeleton help stroke victims regain  use of their legs after a stroke nine  out of ten patients are partially  paralyzed and left with an abnormal gait  the soft robotics device provides  assistance to the joints in the lower  leg the results were immediately visible  with its mechanical help the stroke  victims were able to maintain their  balance and walk similar to the way they  had prior to their paralysis the  patients could walk straight for several  minutes on a treadmill some without the  aid of a handrail  while previous assistive devices have  been made these were bulky and had to be  tethered to a power source this new  exosuit is light enough that could be  used to help an overground therapy as  well not just on a treadmill the  researchers say that while it still  needs long-term testing the assistive  device could bring down the time needed  for rehabilitation after strokes  [Music]
 

